Usage: dockex <command> [container_name] [options]

Available commands:
  info|inspect <container>          - Detailed container info:
      * IP/hostname/OS/command
      * Networks (name/driver/subnet/gateway/IP)
      * CPU shares, memory limit
      * Volumes, env vars, ports, DNS (if running)

  ps [name_pattern]                 - Summarize all containers (CPU/MEM/health/restart).

  logs <container> [lines]          - Show container logs (default: 10 lines).
  logs-errors <container> [lines]   - Show only error-like log lines (default: 500).
  stream_logs <container>           - Stream container logs in real-time.

  start <container>                 - Start a stopped container.
  stop <container>                  - Stop a running container.
  restart <container>               - Restart a container.

  shell <container>                 - Exec into a container (bash, fallback sh).
  exec-run <container> <cmd...>     - Run a one-off command inside a container.
  top <container>                   - Show processes running inside container.

  update_resources <container>      - Update container's CPU and memory limits.

  backup <container>                - Backup a selected volume to a zip file.
  restore <container> <zip>         - Restore container data from a backup zip.

  ports <container>                 - Show published ports for a container.
  dns <container> [hostname]        - Show DNS config / resolve a name inside container.

  benchmark <container> [instances] [requests] [concurrency]
      * instances:   default 3
      * requests:    default 100
      * concurrency: default 10

  stats <container> [duration] [interval]
      * duration:    seconds to profile (default: 30)
      * interval:    seconds between samples (default: 2)

  trace <container> <host-or-url> [port]
      * Run reachability / HTTP probe from inside container.
      * If URL: infer host/port/protocol.
      * If host + port: build http/https URL (443 => https).

  doctor [container]                - Doctor check for Docker host or a container.
      * No container: host + fleet health summary
      * With container: deep health/logs/limits snapshot

  list                              - Show images, containers, networks, volumes.
  nets                              - Show Docker network topology (subnet / containers).
  create <image> [name]             - Interactively create a new container.

  cleanup [unused|aggressive|all]   - Clean up Docker resources (default: unused).
      unused:       Safe cleanup of unused resources.
      aggressive:   Remove all unused resources, including unreferenced images.
      all:          Remove ALL containers/images/volumes/networks (destructive).

Examples:
  dockex info my_container
  dockex ps
  dockex logs my_container 50
  dockex logs-errors my_container 1000
  dockex benchmark my_container 5 500 50
  dockex stats my_container 60 5
  dockex trace my_container api.example.com 443
  dockex dns my_container example.com
  dockex ports my_container
  dockex nets
  dockex doctor my_container
  dockex backup my_container
  dockex create nginx my_nginx
  dockex shell my_container
